s\npopulated here. Full output: `evidence/N90_FINAL_AUDIT/full_suite_rerun.txt`.\n\n## 6. Activation gate (TEST items 6-7)\n\n- N50 status: **PASSED** (original receipt, and reconfirmed live in section 5).\n- N60 status: **NOT_AVAILABLE**. Its own evidence (`results/N60_LIVE_PRODUCT_PROOF.result.v1.md`) shows Codex is live-authenticated (ChatGPT subscription) and both provider hosts are network-reachable, but the Gemini CLI has no usable credential in this environment (`gemini-api-key` auth mode selected, `GEMINI_API_KEY`/`GOOGLE_API_KEY` unset, no Google account signed in) — a real, non-simulated probe failure (exit 41), reproducing the exact prerequisite spec section 20.2 lists (\"provide live credentials/network access for Codex, Gemini...\"). No partial transmission was attempted; no curriculum artifact was produced or claimed. This is an external account/credential gap, not an implementation defect — the runtime, transport, and preflight code all report ready.\n- Therefore: N60 is `NOT_AVAILABLE` solely for a recorded external prerequisite, and N50 passed (both originally and on N90's live rerun). TEST item 7's condition for `IMPLEMENTED_NOT_ACTIVATED` is met. TEST item 6's condition for `ACTIVATED` (authorized live unit + full-release proof) is not met and was not attempted, correctly.\n\n## Findings summary / rework_edges\n\n| Finding | rework_edges key | Owning node | Disposition |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| F1: N40 evidence files had uncommitted post-receipt drift | `evidence_integrity_drift` | N40_CLI_CUTOVER | Resolved by N90 (`git checkout --`, restored to committed state); 0 hash mismatches remain |\n| F2: N40/N50/N60 receipts predate later N20/N30/N31/N32 rework touching graph.py/acceptance.py/repair.py | `receipt_cascade_invalidation` | harness (`prompt_graph_controller.py`), not a curriculum N-node | Closed by direct re-verification (full suite reran clean against current code); non-blocking; recommend harness auto-invalidate descendants on ancestor rewor